# Developing a Hybrid Algorithm that Combine Rule-based and Machine Learning Methods to Detect Social Engineering Attacks

[![DOI](10.5281/zenodo.23961398)
[![Journal](https://journal.hcsr.gov.sy/?p=2147)


Official repository for the research paper **"Developing a Hybrid Algorithm that Combine Rule-based and Machine Learning Methods to Detect Social Engineering Attacks"**, published in the *Syrian Journal for Science and Innovation (SJSI)*, Volume 4, Issue 3 (2026) by **Dana Najeeb** and **Dr. Basel Al-Khatib** (Syrian Virtual University).

## Abstract Overview
The study proposes a hybrid detection algorithm combining automated rule-based methods, dynamic topic blacklists, natural language processing, and machine learning to counter social engineering attacks. Trained and tested on 50,000 Kaggle emails, the model achieved a **97.40%** accuracy rate. 

